WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.369
 Steve, Ryan, congratulations.

00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:05.671
You have forged your
way into the final round

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:06.840
of this competition.

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.641
The first two rounds
you came to our forge

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:11.344
and used our tools and
equipment to forge signature

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:13.479
blades out of salvaged steel.

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:15.248
Now we're sending
you back to your home

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:19.218
forges where you will recreate
an iconic weapon from history.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:25.958
That weapon is the charay.

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:27.727
The history of the
charay sword is deeply

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:30.363
tied to the violent
history of the Khyber Pass,

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:33.299
which separates
Afghanistan and Pakistan.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.935
The sharp, single-edged
blade was a key asset

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.170
of the Afridi tribe.

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:38.871
The charay had
devastating consequences

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:42.475
for the Afridi's enemies because
it could pierce through armor.

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:44.376
The distinctive T
shape of the spine

00:00:44.443 --> 00:00:49.582
gives extra strength to the
charay's razor-sharp blade.

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:51.151
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:54.019 --> 00:00:55.488 line:0%
RYAN: Feels great
being back here

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:57.757 line:0%
in nice, sunny
Jacksonville, Florida.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:01.194
My day-one goal is to actually
get this blade forged.

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:08.167
The only thing I'm
really concerned about

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:11.971
is getting the T back
of the spine correct.

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:17.276
I'm going to create this T spine
by forging in fuller grooves.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:20.946
Getting that correct
is very crucial.

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:22.615
Not good.

00:01:22.681 --> 00:01:26.118
The problem is I put a
little bit too much pressure,

00:01:26.185 --> 00:01:29.088
and it looks like
it's pushed through.

00:01:29.154 --> 00:01:31.391
It's too thin, and
I got a little bit

00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:32.525
of daylight showing in there.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:36.229
So I am going to
have to start over.

00:01:39.031 --> 00:01:42.434 line:0%
STEVE: I was able to
finish up the layering.

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:45.571
I got the overall
dimensions forged out,

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:49.475
but I've never forged a
T into a spine before.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:53.278
If I was in an Afghan
desert, this is probably

00:01:53.345 --> 00:01:58.151
how I would have to do this.

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:02.922
So I drew everything over
length and then just started

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:07.760
to upset that spine, bringing
it out in the shape of a T. I

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.228
think it's working great.

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:12.098
I mean, it's a
nice, even T there.

00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:15.034
Went way quicker than
I thought it would.

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:19.105
It allowed me to get
to the quench today.

00:02:19.171 --> 00:02:21.473
Seems like everything went well.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:26.079
But as I was trying
to pull it out--

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:27.813
[bleep]

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.582
--boom.

00:02:30.649 --> 00:02:31.583
[clang]

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:37.223 line:7%
[bleep]

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:40.360 line:0%
RYAN: After yesterday
having to trash my blade,

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:43.863 line:0%
I really need to get
this blade done today.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.197
So far, so good.

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:47.166
Looking pretty awesome.

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:51.037
Forging in this T joint
is a lot harder than I

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:52.505
thought I was going to be.

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:55.240
So today I'm using
my other option,

00:02:55.307 --> 00:02:57.110
which is the grinding wheel.

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:58.511
This is very crucial.

00:02:58.577 --> 00:03:02.749
I really can't afford to have
to do this blade over again.

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:05.384
As I'm grinding in the T, I
notice that it's standing out

00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:07.220
way better than I ever thought.

00:03:07.286 --> 00:03:09.255
I can control it a lot better.

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:11.123
Everything's getting
a lot lighter,

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.459
and I am very happy
at this point.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.896
STEVE: When I was quenching,
obviously the blade

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:20.767
fell, but I got lucky.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:21.968
Everything's fine.

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:25.672
So I'd like to get through some
testing early this morning.

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:30.209
Failure during testing
here would give me only 14,

00:03:30.275 --> 00:03:33.312
15 hours to build
a complete charay.

00:03:33.378 --> 00:03:35.215
So I don't need a failure here.

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:42.422
Oh yeah.

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:48.328
Ate that up,
absolutely no problem.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.633 line:0%
RYAN: This blade
looks extremely sexy.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.034
Now I'm just going
to concentrate

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:58.771
on doing my handle
scales, inlays, cleaning

00:03:58.804 --> 00:04:00.006
up the blade a lot more.

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:04.577
And I decide I want to carve
a wolf head in the front of it

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:08.313
just to kind of set it
apart, make it stand out.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.984
My wolf looks badass.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:11.851
The blade's sharp.

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:12.918
The blade's strong.

00:04:12.985 --> 00:04:14.753
It's time to test it.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:17.857
All right, here we go.

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:21.761
[banging]

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:27.199
It's pretty good.

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:29.368
There's no edge
damage or anything.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.469
Just bring it on, man.

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:32.971
Do whatever you want to do.

00:04:33.038 --> 00:04:34.206
Awesome.

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:37.844
 Bladesmiths, the
charay was a weapon known

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.813
to be light, fast, and sharp.

00:04:40.879 --> 00:04:43.316
To see what kind of lethal
damage your weapon can do,

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:45.918
I will take your charay and
deliver slashes and stabs

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:47.453
on this ballistics dummy.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.521
Steve, you're up first.

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:49.088
You ready?

00:04:49.121 --> 00:04:49.922
 Absolutely.

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:51.223
DOUG: Let's do this.

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:54.794
[music playing]

00:05:07.239 --> 00:05:10.309
Well, Steve, I like
the Damascus pattern.

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:13.212
And overall, it's got
a great fit and finish.

00:05:13.278 --> 00:05:16.448
Your edge definitely lacerated.

00:05:16.515 --> 00:05:18.651
It even cut into the rib.

00:05:18.685 --> 00:05:21.420
On the slash, it lacerates
and has a deep thrust

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:25.624
and allows me to disembowel
this ballistics dummy.

00:05:25.691 --> 00:05:27.326
Your blade, sir, will kill.

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:28.794
- Thank you.
- Ryan, you're next.

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:29.361
You ready?

00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:30.396
 Yeah, man.

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:34.567
[music playing]

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:47.213
 Well, Ryan, let's
talk about your blade.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.615
For a charay, it is heavy.

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:53.819
But it's sharp enough
to lacerate and dig in,

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:57.155
and the thrust allows
for a laceration out.

00:05:57.222 --> 00:05:59.992
Your blade, sir, will kill.

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.094
 All right, gentlemen.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.595
Now, to test the
sharpness of your blade,

00:06:02.661 --> 00:06:05.164
I'll be cutting through these
racks of sugar cane forehand

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:06.432
and backhand.

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:09.001
What I want to see is a
clean cut with very little

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:11.304
resistance to that blade.

00:06:11.337 --> 00:06:12.371
Steve, you're up first.

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:13.873
You ready?
- Yes, sir.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:14.407
 OK.

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:17.510
[music playing]

00:06:24.783 --> 00:06:27.587
All right, well, it felt
good cutting with this.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.388
You can see these
first cuts very clean.

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:32.825
The second cut I kind of
blew through this one.

00:06:32.891 --> 00:06:36.295
You can actually see where the
T back smacked that sucker.

00:06:36.362 --> 00:06:38.864
Now, that's typical
of this shape blade.

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:39.665
Well done.

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:40.432
 Thank you.

00:06:40.499 --> 00:06:41.466
 All right, Ryan, you're up.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:42.468
You ready for this?

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:44.170
 Do me proud.

00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:47.073
[music playing]

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:54.614
 So, Ryan, first off, there's
a lot of weight in this play.

00:06:54.647 --> 00:06:57.517
That T back is there
to take weight out.

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:59.518
But everything's
still right and tight.

00:06:59.584 --> 00:07:02.355
It obviously cut pretty well.

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:03.522
Cut two of these canes.

00:07:03.588 --> 00:07:05.491
Kind of just mash that
one out of the way,

00:07:05.557 --> 00:07:08.327
but you can see the
cut in there is clean.

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:10.596
I like the decorative
pieces, you know,

00:07:10.663 --> 00:07:12.965
this wolf's head here.

00:07:13.032 --> 00:07:14.399
All in all, she's a cutter.

00:07:14.466 --> 00:07:17.236
It's definitely sharp.

00:07:17.303 --> 00:07:18.236
All right, gentlemen.

00:07:18.303 --> 00:07:19.705
Next up-- the strength test.

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:22.074
It's the bullet test,
so let's clear the range

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:23.209
and get this set.

00:07:23.275 --> 00:07:25.845
Now we've got your blade,
Steve, locked into a vise.

00:07:25.912 --> 00:07:28.080
We're going to fire one
round right at that edge.

00:07:28.146 --> 00:07:31.984
If everything's good, it
should split that bullet fine.

00:07:32.018 --> 00:07:33.052
You ready for this?

00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:33.986
 Yes, sir.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.254
 OK.

00:07:35.288 --> 00:07:39.158
3, 2, 1, fire.

00:07:39.225 --> 00:07:40.125
[gun shot]

00:07:40.159 --> 00:07:43.596
[music playing]

00:07:46.332 --> 00:07:47.600
 Oh, look at that.

00:07:49.935 --> 00:07:53.506
 Well, you've still
got an edge there.

00:07:53.573 --> 00:07:57.075 line:0%
You can actually see right
where the bullet spun

00:07:57.142 --> 00:07:58.210 line:7%
down the side of that blade.

00:07:58.277 --> 00:08:01.547 line:0%
You can see where it caught
the T back on that side.

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:04.750
But I think you made a
beautiful piece here,

00:08:04.816 --> 00:08:07.052
and it certainly
held up in that test.

00:08:07.119 --> 00:08:08.153
 Thank you, sir.

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:09.588
 All right, Ryan, you're up.

00:08:09.655 --> 00:08:10.422
Are you ready for this?

00:08:10.489 --> 00:08:12.324
 Let's do it.

00:08:12.391 --> 00:08:16.462
 3, 2, 1, fire.

00:08:16.529 --> 00:08:19.565
[gun shot]

00:08:23.235 --> 00:08:24.871
 Damn.

00:08:24.937 --> 00:08:26.839
 That was [bleep].

00:08:26.906 --> 00:08:29.608
 All right, Ryan, I don't
see any damage at all.

00:08:29.674 --> 00:08:32.478
That bullet painted
your blade pretty good.

00:08:32.544 --> 00:08:35.447
Didn't touch the T
back on this side.

00:08:35.514 --> 00:08:37.149 line:0%
Kind of caught a little
bit on that side.

00:08:37.216 --> 00:08:41.386 line:0%
But all in all, there's
zero edge damage there.

00:08:41.453 --> 00:08:42.321
Nicely done.

00:08:42.388 --> 00:08:44.122
 Thank you, sir.

00:08:44.156 --> 00:08:47.626
 Bladesmiths, these
decisions are always tough,

00:08:47.692 --> 00:08:49.695
but the judges have made one.

00:08:49.762 --> 00:08:51.397
There can only be
one "Forged in Fire"

00:08:51.463 --> 00:08:53.698
champion in this
arena of competition,

00:08:53.765 --> 00:09:00.039
and that champion is Steve.

00:09:00.106 --> 00:09:00.973
Congratulations.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.074
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:03.141 --> 00:09:04.276
 Thank you.

00:09:04.309 --> 00:09:08.381
 Ryan, I have to ask you,
please surrender your weapon.

00:09:08.447 --> 00:09:11.417
 Forged in Fire" champion would
have meant the world to me,

00:09:11.484 --> 00:09:13.719
but you just really have
to be on your A game.

00:09:13.786 --> 00:09:14.920
You know, no matter
what it takes,

00:09:14.987 --> 00:09:16.588
you just got to
pull out all stops.

00:09:16.655 --> 00:09:17.990
You got to make sure
to look at the finer

00:09:18.023 --> 00:09:23.462
details, and yeah, that's
what it takes to win this.

00:09:23.529 --> 00:09:24.629
 Steve, congratulations.

00:09:24.663 --> 00:09:25.898
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:09:25.964 --> 00:09:29.902
and that's a title that
comes with $10,000.

00:09:29.969 --> 00:09:30.836
Good job.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:31.369
[applause]

00:09:31.436 --> 00:09:33.038
 Thank you.

00:09:33.105 --> 00:09:34.139
Thank you.

00:09:34.206 --> 00:09:35.708
 Steve, your blade was
light and well constructed,

00:09:35.774 --> 00:09:37.376
and it did wonderfully
in the tests.

00:09:37.443 --> 00:09:38.911
And also the fact
this is the first time

00:09:38.978 --> 00:09:41.246
you've done a T back, it makes
it that much more impressive.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:42.381
Well done.

00:09:42.448 --> 00:09:44.983
STEVE: I am a "Forged
in Fire champion.

00:09:45.017 --> 00:09:47.253
Yay!

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:50.122
I came here to prove that
I can compete with some

00:09:50.189 --> 00:09:53.492
of the best smiths in
the world and beat them,

00:09:53.559 --> 00:09:55.127
and I did just that.

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:55.995
[laughs]

00:09:56.062 --> 00:09:59.732
[music playing]

